WEBVTT

1

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:33.333

I doubt this is something you want

to hear, but just listen.



2

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.958

Three years ago...



3

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:40.167

Back then, we still might've been able

to change something.



4

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.208

"3 Years Ago"



5

00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:51.500

Captain! The team that went ashore

hasn't made contact for two hours!



6

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.417

Hmm. Prepare to send teams two and three.



7

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:56.708

Yes, sir!



8

00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:01.292

This island of devils defeated the Warrior unit.



9

00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:05.458

Whatever the cost,

Marley must learn what happened.



10

00:01:09.292 --> 00:01:11.375

Hang on!



11

00:01:13.292 --> 00:01:16.833

I-It's a devil!



12

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:38.292

Hello, friends from Marley!

Welcome to Paradis Island!



13

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:44.417

I'm Hange, here to greet our guests

who've come so far across the sea!



14

00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:48.458

Now, step this way and join us for some tea!



15

00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:54.792

By the way, we're already friends

with this guest that arrived before you!



16

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:58.458

Isn't that right, Nicolo?!



17

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:03.542

Captain! Forget about me

and shoot these devils!



18

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:06.167

--What are you saying, Nicolo?!



19

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.167

--Captain!

--What are you saying, Nicolo?!



20

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:11.250

He's tired of your shitty skit.



21

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:18.500

Nicolo! Understand this, you devils!

Marley doesn't mingle with filthy blood!



22

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.042

Go drink your pig piss with your filthy friends!



23

00:02:22.042 --> 00:02:27.000

Aww! Hey! You sure you wanna be rude to us?!



24

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.792

Can't you see the Titan behind you?!



25

00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:40.458

We'll never yield to you devils!

Say hello to this!



26

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:54.917

Hands up, Yelena!



27

00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:57.292

Drop your weapons.



28

00:02:57.292 --> 00:02:58.542

What are you...?



29

00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:00.625

Do as she says.



30

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:04.625

Hange, I'd be happy to accept your invitation.



31

00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:06.750

Let's have tea.



32

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:14.917

I've longed to meet you, Eren.



33

00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:49.958

"Brave Volunteers"



34

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:55.125

That huge lady of theirs

shot and killed her comrade.



35

00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:57.083

Wonder what her goal is.



36

00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:01.750

Who knows? Whether friend or foe,

she's not to be trusted.



37

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.292

No napping, Sasha.



38

00:05:03.292 --> 00:05:09.333

But their willingness to share

information is unbelievably lucky for us.



39

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:12.875

Yeah, we've been really lucky.



40

00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:16.250

We stopped their landing by pure chance.



41

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.375

If Marley comes in force, we'll be screwed.



42

00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:22.208

We've gotta do something.



43

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:31.042

Ah, I see! That's how it shoots a bunch!



44

00:05:31.042 --> 00:05:35.458

That's standard-issue in Marley.



45

00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:39.667

The Marley army has

20,000 soldiers per division.



46

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:43.625

With 50 divisions, that's 1,000,000 soldiers.



47

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:49.250

There's also the navy with three fleets,

each comprised of 21 battleships.



48

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:54.792

They've made tremendous progress in

new weapons and aerial warfare as well.



49

00:05:54.792 --> 00:05:56.542

Aerial...?



50

00:05:56.542 --> 00:05:57.792

Tsk!



51

00:05:57.792 --> 00:06:00.750

Don't freak out or they'll think we're weak.



52

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:01.833

I know!



53

00:06:01.833 --> 00:06:07.167

In other words, vehicles allowing one

to attack the enemy from the sky.



54

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:08.625

Huh?! From the sky?!



55

00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:10.500

Hey!



56

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:19.042

If Marley had such capabilities this whole time,

why haven't they attacked in over a year?



57

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:21.625

There are two main reasons.



58

00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:24.792

One being the Pure Titans released here.



59

00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:30.917

Even with the latest weapons,

they would hinder a land assault.



60

00:06:30.917 --> 00:06:35.292

They were used as a tool to

confine Eldians within the walls,



61

00:06:35.292 --> 00:06:39.833

but in turn, they've protected

Eldia from invasion.



62

00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:43.083

Yeah. Well, ain't that funny?



63

00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:48.625

Though dawn is coming soon,

and that's when Titans are active.



64

00:06:48.625 --> 00:06:53.500

But if we're way out here,

sipping on tea outside the walls,



65

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:58.125

you must have killed all

the Titans roaming around.



66

00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:00.375

Is that true?



67

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:05.000

And what if it is?

You gonna report it to Marley?



68

00:07:06.542 --> 00:07:11.167

No, it blows away my expectations.



69

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:13.500

And the second reason?



70

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.750

Currently, Marley is at war

with multiple nations.



71

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.917

They can't be bothered with Paradis.



72

00:07:20.917 --> 00:07:24.833

You defeated the Warrior unit,

the pride of Marley,



73

00:07:24.833 --> 00:07:30.667

and captured two of their main weapons,

the Colossal and Female Titans.



74

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:39.083

Marley's many enemies took notice

and were quick to unite and declare war.



75

00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:43.875

If you guys are secret agents

who infiltrated Marley,



76

00:07:43.875 --> 00:07:48.125

I'm guessing you came

from conquered nations?



77

00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:56.208

Oh, I'm right?! If you're going up against

Marley, I bet you've got big backers!



78

00:07:57.125 --> 00:08:01.833

We're not secret agents or anything of the sort.



79

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:08.000

We were powerless. Marley took our

homes and forced us to be soldiers.



80

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.750

We were close to losing hope

at ever striking back.



81

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.208

Until we met him.



82

00:08:17.167 --> 00:08:21.917

A Titan that people of the

world feared, calling it a devil.



83

00:08:21.917 --> 00:08:25.083

But I saw something completely different...



84

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:31.542

A god. One that gave hope

to the powerless.



85

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:38.958

Under Zeke Jaeger's command,

we shot our superiors.



86

00:08:38.958 --> 00:08:46.083

We're the Anti-Marleyan Volunteers.

Our goal: To free the Eldian people.



87

00:08:47.417 --> 00:08:50.792

That concludes Zeke Jaeger's requests.



88

00:08:50.792 --> 00:08:54.708

For the sake of all Eldians

whose existence is threatened--



89

00:08:54.708 --> 00:08:57.792

Absurd! I don't even want to hear it!



90

00:08:57.792 --> 00:08:59.833

He's the Beast Titan!



91

00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:04.000

He turned the people of Ragako

into Titans and incited a panic!



92

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:09.125

This is the same person who

nearly annihilated the Scouts!



93

00:09:09.125 --> 00:09:13.833

His one and only goal is to

retake the Founding Titan.



94

00:09:13.833 --> 00:09:18.792

Since he can't do it by force,

he'll attempt it diplomatically.



95

00:09:18.792 --> 00:09:25.708

He should know we'll expect that.

Let's hear what else he has to say.



96

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:31.208

According to Zeke, he has a secret

plan to solve the Eldian issue.



97

00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:37.750

To carry it out, it requires the Founding

Titan and a Titan with royal blood.



98

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.792

With both, the world can be saved.



99

00:09:40.792 --> 00:09:46.458

However, he will only reveal the plan

when his conditions are met.



100

00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:47.583

Bullshit!



101

00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:50.500

He must think we're idiots!



102

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.458

Eren?



103

00:09:51.458 --> 00:09:55.250

He's telling the truth. I remember...



104

00:09:55.250 --> 00:10:00.292

The one time I was able to use

the Founding Titan's power



105

00:10:00.292 --> 00:10:04.792

was when I touched a Titan with royal blood.



106

00:10:04.792 --> 00:10:11.208

That Titan had to be my father's

other wife, Dina Fritz.



107

00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:18.250

Zeke, Dina's son, must have figured out

a way to elude the vow renouncing war.



108

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:22.833

The one single hope remaining for us Eldians:



109

00:10:22.833 --> 00:10:30.000

To wake the millions of Titans sleeping

in the walls and activate the rumbling.



110

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.417

You... Why did you keep quiet

about this for so long?



111

00:10:35.417 --> 00:10:38.667

I was concerned for Historia's safety.



112

00:10:38.667 --> 00:10:44.875

I couldn't let her get made into a Titan

based on some hunch of mine.



113

00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:47.542

Yeah, it was careless of me.



114

00:10:47.542 --> 00:10:49.375

We'll talk about it later.



115

00:10:49.375 --> 00:10:55.292

But if that's really true,

Zeke's secret plan holds up.



116

00:10:55.292 --> 00:10:57.958

Are you nuts?! You trust them?!



117

00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:02.083

Yeah! We can't have all those

soldiers on the island!



118

00:11:02.083 --> 00:11:04.958

We oughta hang 'em all!



119

00:11:04.958 --> 00:11:07.542

No, we can't do that.



120

00:11:07.542 --> 00:11:13.917

To protect the island from Marley's

scout ships, we need the volunteers.



121

00:11:13.917 --> 00:11:17.083

Without their "wireless radio"...



122

00:11:17.083 --> 00:11:21.000

This is... fir... scout fleet. Request... aid.



123

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.625

This is... first scout fleet.



124

00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:25.875

Second fleet. Go ahead.



125

00:11:25.875 --> 00:11:31.417

What a relief! Our ship ran aground!

We've been waiting for your help.



126

00:11:31.417 --> 00:11:34.792

We're on the way! In the cove, huh?



127

00:11:34.792 --> 00:11:39.583

How many ships? Don't worry!

Two are headed your way!



128

00:11:40.542 --> 00:11:41.917

Hey!



129

00:11:41.917 --> 00:11:45.000

You okay?! We're coming to get you!



130

00:11:47.708 --> 00:11:50.625

--It's the Colossal Titan!

--How?!



131

00:11:52.042 --> 00:11:54.083

Hey! It's the enemy!



132

00:11:54.083 --> 00:11:55.583

Hurry! Jump!



133

00:11:55.583 --> 00:11:56.542

Run!



134

00:11:56.542 --> 00:11:58.333

Jump off!



135

00:12:03.167 --> 00:12:08.417

Welcome to the filthy island of

filthy devils. You're gonna love it.



136

00:12:08.417 --> 00:12:11.083

As long as you like pig piss.



137

00:12:11.083 --> 00:12:14.583

You can leave if you want, but not on a ship.



138

00:12:14.583 --> 00:12:17.250

Are you good at swimming?



139

00:12:18.208 --> 00:12:21.167

It was fun back then.



140

00:12:21.167 --> 00:12:27.500

Certainly, we Eldians are feared

and hated by the world.



141

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:32.042

By people across the sea

whose faces we don't know.



142

00:12:32.042 --> 00:12:37.333

But not everyone across the sea

was our enemy.



143

00:12:37.333 --> 00:12:45.042

And we found out the world itself

was complex and full of unknowns.



144

00:12:45.042 --> 00:12:49.917

By the way, why do you have

dark skin, Onyankopon?



145

00:12:50.875 --> 00:12:57.667

Because our creator thought, "It's more

interesting with a mix of people."



146

00:12:57.667 --> 00:13:04.375

You Subjects of Ymir are the same.

We exist because we were wanted.



147

00:13:04.375 --> 00:13:06.792

Who created us?



148

00:13:06.792 --> 00:13:13.250

The one who gave the

Founder Ymir power. God.



149

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:18.708

That's what some people believe.

Aren't we free to think what we want?



150

00:13:23.542 --> 00:13:26.000

What the hell is this food?



151

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.917

Is it even edible?



152

00:13:27.917 --> 00:13:29.042

Smells fishy.



153

00:13:29.042 --> 00:13:34.125

You've never had seafood?

Nicolo's a master of Marleyan cooking.



154

00:13:34.125 --> 00:13:39.083

Jerks. If you don't like it, don't eat.

Eldians like you don't--



155

00:13:42.625 --> 00:13:45.375

So good!



156

00:13:45.375 --> 00:13:47.542

--Hey!

--No fair, Sasha!



157

00:13:49.125 --> 00:13:54.250

Nicolo! You're a food genius!



158

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.875

S-Stop eating like a pig!



159

00:13:56.875 --> 00:14:00.208

I've never had anything like this!



160

00:14:01.333 --> 00:14:04.250

There's plenty, so take your time.



161

00:14:10.167 --> 00:14:13.208

The port will be finished soon!



162

00:14:13.208 --> 00:14:17.750

Thanks to the Marleyan engineers,

building it's been quick.



163

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.333

They've sure been cooperative.



164

00:14:21.125 --> 00:14:26.042

It went bad at first since

neither side trusted the other.



165

00:14:26.042 --> 00:14:32.833

But given enough time, if we set aside

our labels and see each other as people,



166

00:14:32.833 --> 00:14:35.208

we can understand each other.



167

00:14:36.667 --> 00:14:40.125

Armin. Have you seen Bertholdt's memories?



168

00:14:40.125 --> 00:14:45.417

Huh? Yeah, but there's

nothing that seems helpful.



169

00:14:45.417 --> 00:14:50.208

There's not much time.

Zeke has less than three years left.



170

00:14:50.208 --> 00:14:53.167

Yeah, about that...



171

00:14:53.167 --> 00:14:57.458

Do we really want to go along

with Yelena's plan?



172

00:14:57.458 --> 00:14:59.167

What's the problem?



173

00:14:59.167 --> 00:15:05.542

Is using the rumbling to threaten the

world the only way to protect Eldians?



174

00:15:05.542 --> 00:15:10.542

Then we <i>will </i>be the devils

that terrorize the world.



175

00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:13.792

Before it comes to that, can't we talk?



176

00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:17.792

If we can fix Marley and the

world's misconception...



177

00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:21.708

Misconception? What misconception?



178

00:15:21.708 --> 00:15:24.375

You know, like how we're scary.



179

00:15:24.375 --> 00:15:31.708

The world sees us as monsters who can

turn into Titans. They're not wrong.



180

00:15:31.708 --> 00:15:34.625

There're Marleyans who like us, too.



181

00:15:34.625 --> 00:15:36.500

How many?



182

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:40.625

Most of the Marleyans

are sitting in prison cells.



183

00:15:40.625 --> 00:15:43.333

But given enough time...



184

00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:47.125

Yeah. We need time.



185

00:15:48.042 --> 00:15:54.375

That's right. And to buy us that time,

we've gotta keep 'em at bay.



186

00:15:59.458 --> 00:16:04.875

I wonder... did we make the right choice?



187

00:16:06.792 --> 00:16:14.292

I can't help but think:

Could there have been some other path?



188

00:16:14.292 --> 00:16:20.917

I thought I understood Eren

better than anyone. Even Mikasa.



189

00:16:20.917 --> 00:16:24.042

But I don't know anymore.



190

00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:29.917

"The Scout Fleet was formed to investigate

Paradis Island after the Operation to Retake

the Founding Titan had failed. Not a single one

has returned to Marley to this day."



191

00:16:38.167 --> 00:16:43.083

Hey! Aren't you a Marleyan?!

What the hell are you doing here?!



192

00:16:43.083 --> 00:16:46.292

--This graveyard is full of people

your kind killed!



193

00:16:46.292 --> 00:16:47.458

--Wait!

--This graveyard is full of people

your kind killed!



194

00:16:47.458 --> 00:16:50.708

Let us take care of this guy!



195

00:16:50.708 --> 00:16:53.458

Sorry. Please.



196

00:16:53.458 --> 00:16:55.917

Marleyans can piss off!



197

00:16:55.917 --> 00:16:56.917

Hey, Nicolo!



198

00:16:56.917 --> 00:16:58.958

You okay?



199

00:16:58.958 --> 00:17:02.167

Dammit! Why?!



200

00:17:03.333 --> 00:17:06.708

Sasha's really dead?



201

00:17:06.708 --> 00:17:08.250

Yeah.



202

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.750

Why? What the hell were you guys doing?!



203

00:17:16.625 --> 00:17:20.375

Shot by a kid who sneaked on the airship?



204

00:17:21.708 --> 00:17:25.333

It's too ridiculous to be true.



205

00:17:25.333 --> 00:17:29.833

It was no ordinary girl. She'd been trained.



206

00:17:29.833 --> 00:17:31.958

A Warrior candidate?



207

00:17:31.958 --> 00:17:36.042

I let my guard down. Sorry.



208

00:17:36.042 --> 00:17:41.708

Why apologize to me?

All I did was cook her food.



209

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:50.500

Thanks for letting her eat

so much tasty food, Nicolo.



210

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:54.625

What do you think about this, Conny?



211

00:17:54.625 --> 00:17:59.417

Sasha and I were like twins.



212

00:17:59.417 --> 00:18:02.958

It feels like half of me is gone.



213

00:18:05.125 --> 00:18:07.167

You're...



214

00:18:07.167 --> 00:18:10.375

Y'all knew my daughter, did ya?



215

00:18:18.167 --> 00:18:20.500

U-Um...



216

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:26.458

I'm just a captive Marleyan,

but I'm allowed to work as a chef.



217

00:18:26.458 --> 00:18:31.458

Your daughter loved eating my

food more than anyone else.



218

00:18:31.458 --> 00:18:38.375

So... if you ever want to...

please come and eat my food.



219

00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:46.125

On the house, right?



220

00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:47.750

Of course.



221

00:18:54.917 --> 00:19:01.250

You guys are calling it a victory.

Isn't ignorance a scary thing?



222

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:06.792

If I send your dead body to Marley

and reveal your little plot,



223

00:19:06.792 --> 00:19:09.625

your gramps and granny are done for.



224

00:19:09.625 --> 00:19:15.875

But if this secret plan of yours is real,

I can wait to chop you up.



225

00:19:15.875 --> 00:19:18.625

Either way works for me.



226

00:19:18.625 --> 00:19:25.583

I appreciate your graciousness.

But don't I get to meet Eren first?



227

00:19:25.583 --> 00:19:30.625

Don't be in such a hurry.

We've got the finest hotel for you.



228

00:19:30.625 --> 00:19:34.333

You can stay there and relax a while.



229

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:41.000

Hey... Can you please stop glaring at me?



230

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:45.708

This is all of the Titan serum

we stole from Marley.



231

00:19:45.708 --> 00:19:48.833

But you'll have trouble reproducing it.



232

00:19:48.833 --> 00:19:52.833

No, we should manage fine with this much.



233

00:19:52.833 --> 00:19:57.042

I only wish we could properly thank you.



234

00:19:57.042 --> 00:20:02.750

We owe you so much already.

We were ignorant, but you gave us hope.



235

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:08.042

For us to suspect you,

we're truly no better than devils.



236

00:20:08.042 --> 00:20:14.333

For three years, we've done nothing

but show we're friends of the Eldians.



237

00:20:14.333 --> 00:20:22.375

It's unfortunate. The guns we brought

were meant to give Eldians freedom.



238

00:20:22.375 --> 00:20:29.208

I know it's selfish to ask, but can you

overlook our cautiousness for a while?



239

00:20:29.208 --> 00:20:32.750

We have to keep Zeke on a tight leash.



240

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:39.792

It's fine, Commander Pyxis.

We'll dine at the same table again soon.



241

00:20:40.958 --> 00:20:43.750

<i>This </i>is my hotel?



242

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.375

You got a problem with it?



243

00:20:46.375 --> 00:20:51.625

It's a forest of giant trees.

I can't think of a better place for you.



244

00:20:51.625 --> 00:20:55.500

Might be lots of fun with ODM gear.



245

00:20:55.500 --> 00:21:01.583

Hey, Captain Levi. Think I could show

Gabi and Falco this natural wonder?



246

00:21:01.583 --> 00:21:03.208

Tsk.



247

00:21:03.208 --> 00:21:08.292

Whether they see the sights

or not depends on you.



248

00:21:15.458 --> 00:21:19.625

Eren... Jaeger!



249

00:21:19.625 --> 00:21:23.042

Eren would have done it alone.



250

00:21:23.042 --> 00:21:29.250

Whether we helped him or not,

the worst would've happened anyways.



251

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:33.333

In any case, we killed a lot of people.



252

00:21:33.333 --> 00:21:37.417

The navy, army, and civilians

got dragged into it.



253

00:21:37.417 --> 00:21:41.917

And just like that, all were lost.



254

00:21:41.917 --> 00:21:45.292

But unless that port was destroyed,



255

00:21:45.292 --> 00:21:50.250

Marley would've retaliated

and attacked the island.



256

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:56.042

We killed any hope for peace,

but we had no choice.



257

00:21:56.042 --> 00:22:00.167

Just like you guys that day.



258

00:22:00.167 --> 00:22:03.875

Hey, Annie...



259

00:22:03.875 --> 00:22:06.875

Say something, please.



260

00:22:09.542 --> 00:22:12.000

Fight or die.



261

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.875

Win... and live.



262

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.542

The only way to win is to fight.



263

00:22:25.542 --> 00:22:27.833

Fight.



264

00:22:27.833 --> 00:22:29.542

Fight!



265

00:24:02.667 --> 00:24:08.833

Without any allies on the outside,

they must kill their enemies to live.



266

00:24:08.833 --> 00:24:14.583

Is that the right choice or not?

There's not a soul who knows.



267

00:24:14.583 --> 00:24:17.046

Next episode: "A Sound Argument."

